    "objectID": "getting-started/02-create-workspace.html",
    "href": "getting-started/02-create-workspace.html",
    "title": "Create your personal workspace",
    "section": "",
    "text": "Workspace template: TO BE LINKED\n\n\nCreate a GitHub account.\nOpen the workspace template repository.\nSelect Use this template → Create a new repository.\nCreate your repository as Private.\nOpen Code → Codespaces → Create codespace on main.\nWait for the environment to finish its first initialization.\n\nThe first initialization can take a few minutes.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Getting started",
      "Create your personal workspace"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "getting-started/04-save-sync-stop.html",
    "href": "getting-started/04-save-sync-stop.html",
    "title": "Save, sync and stop",
    "section": "",
    "text": "ImportantAlways stop your Codespace when you finish\n\n\n\nClosing the browser tab is not the same as stopping the Codespace.\n\n\nBefore leaving:\n\nSave all notebooks and files.\nCommit your changes.\nSync them with GitHub.\nVerify the repository on GitHub.\nStop the Codespace.\n\nYour GitHub repository is the permanent copy of your work.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Getting started",
      "Save, sync and stop"
    ]
  },
